abelian group of order n and Davenport constant D, and put m = n + D − 1. Let x = (x1,. . .,xm) ∈ Gm. Gao's theorem states that there is a reordering (xj1, . . ., xjm) of x such that\nLet w = (x1, . . ., wm) ∈ ℤm. As a corollary of the main result, we show that there are reorderings (xj1, . . ., xjm) of x and (wk1, . . ., wkm) of w, such that\nwhere xj1 is the most repeated value in x. For w = (1, . . ., 1), this result reduces to Gao's theorem.\n\nTopics\n\nNo keywords indexed for this article. Browse by subject →\n\nReferences\n\n12\n\n[1]\n\n10.1016/j.disc.2004.02.001\n\n[2]\n\n10.1007/s00493-006-0025-y\n\n[3]\n\n10.1017/s0963548300001723\n\n[4]\n\nScherk \"Advanced problems and solutions: Solutions 4466\" Amer. Math. Monthly (1955)\n\n[5]\n\n10.1112/jlms/s1-22.2.85\n\n[6]\n\n10.1016/0012-365x(94)00308-6\n\n[7]\n\n10.1016/s1385-7258(56)50032-7\n\n[8]\n\nErdős \"A theorem in additive number theory\" Bull Res. Council Israel (1961)\n\n[9]\n\n10.1016/0012-365x(92)90267-j\n\n[10]\n\n10.1006/jnth.1996.0067\n\n[11]\n\nGeroldinger (2006)\n\n[12]\n\nErdős \"On the addition of residue classes mod p\" Acta Arith. (1964) 10.4064/aa-9-2-149-159\n\nCited By\n\n8\n\nOn zero-sum subsequences of prescribed length\n\nDongchun Han, Hanbin ZHANG · 2017\n\nInternational Journal of Number The...\n\nOn zero-sum subsequences of lengthkexp(G)\n\nWeidong Gao, Dongchun Han · 2014\n\nJournal of Combinatorial Theory, Se...\n\nMetrics\n\n8\n\nCitations\n\n12\n\nReferences\n\nDetails\n\nPublished\n    Nov 01, 2008\n\nVol/Issue\n    17(6)\n\nPages\n    793-798\n\nLicense\n    View\n\nAuthors\n\nY YAHYA O. HAMIDOUNE\n\nCite This Article\n\nYAHYA O. HAMIDOUNE (2008). A Weighted Generalization of Gao's n + D − 1 Theorem. Combinatorics, Probability and Computing, 17(6), 793-798. https://doi.org/10.1017/s0963548308009425--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nau:Grynkiewicz_D in:math - SciRate Search (https://scirate.com/search?q=au%3AGrynkiewicz_D+in%3Amath)\nciteturn1search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; ~Ordaz}, title = {{R}epresentation of {F}inite {A}belian {G}roup {E}lements by {S}ubsequence {S}ums}, year = {2008}, eprint = {0806.0309}, note = {arXiv:0806.0309v1} }[Button: Copy Citation] ... A conjecture of Hamidoune says that if $W=w_1... w_n$ is a sequence of integers, all but at most one relatively prime to $|G|$, and $S$ is a sequence over $G$ with $|S|\\geq |W|+|G|-1\\geq |G|+1$, the maximum multiplicity of $S$ at most $|W|$, and $\\sigma(W)\\equiv 0\\mod |G|$, then there exists a nontrivial subgroup $H$ such that every element $g\\in H$ can be represented as a weighted subsequence sum of the form $g=\\sum_{i=1}^{n}w_is_i$, with $s_1... s_n$ a subsequence of $S$.\n  * Representation of Finite Abelian Group Elements by Subsequence Sums\n\nD. J. Grynkiewicz, E. Marchan, O. Ordaz\n\nJun 03 2008 math.NT math.CO arXiv:0806.0309v1\n\n[Button: Scited][Button: Scite!]\n\n0\n\n@misc{0806.0309, author = {D.~J.~Grynkiewicz and E.~Marchan and O.~Ordaz}, title = {{R}epresentation of {F}inite {A}belian {G}roup {E}lements by {S}ubsequence {S}ums}, year = {2008}, eprint = {0806.0309}, note = {arXiv:0806.0309v1} }[Button: Copy Citation]\n\nPDF\n\nLet $G\\cong C_{n_1}\\oplus ... \\oplus C_{n_r}$ be a finite and nontrivial abelian group with $n_1|n_2|...|n_r$. A conjecture of Hamidoune says that if $W=w_1... w_n$ is a sequence of integers, all but at most one relatively prime to $|G|$, and $S$ is a sequence over $G$ with $|S|\\geq |W|+|G|-1\\geq |G|+1$, the maximum multiplicity of $S$ at most $|W|$, and $\\sigma(W)\\equiv 0\\mod |G|$, then there exists a nontrivial subgroup $H$ such that every element $g\\in H$ can be represented as a weighted subsequence sum of the form $g=\\sum_{i=1}^{n}w_is_i$, with $s_1... s_n$ a subsequence of $S$. We give two examples showing this does not hold in general, and characterize the counterexamples for large $|W|\\geq {1/2}|G|$. A theorem of Gao, generalizing an older result of Olson, says that if $G$ is a finite abelian group, and $S$ is a sequence over $G$ with $|S|\\geq |G|+D(G)-1$, then either every element of $G$ can be represented as a $|G|$-term subsequence sum from $S$, or there exists a coset $g+H$ such that all but at most $|G/H|-2$ terms of $S$ are from $g+H$. We establish some very special cases in a weighted analog of this theorem conjectured by Ordaz and Quiroz, and some partial conclusions in the remaining cases, which imply a recent result of Ordaz and Quiroz. This is done, in part, by extending a weighted setpartition theorem of Grynkiewicz, which we then use to also improve the previously mentioned result of Gao by showing that the hypothesis $|S|\\geq |G|+D(G)-1$ can be relaxed to $|S|\\geq |G|+d^*(G)$, where $d^*(G)=\\Sum_{i=1}^{r}(n_i-1)$. We also use this method to derive a variation on Hamidoune's conjecture valid when at least $d^*(G)$ of the $w_i$ are relatively prime to $|G|$.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nStructural additive theory. Based on courses given at Karl-Franzens-Universität Graz, Austria, 2008–2012 (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/266860083_Structural_additive_theory_Based_on_courses_given_at_Karl-Franzens-Universitat_Graz_Austria_2008-2012)\nciteturn1search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 13.9 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; When = −1, Vosper's theorem [37,Theorem 8.1] [16] implies that Conjecture 1.2 holds without restriction. When = 0, Hamidoune and Rodseth [19] established Conjecture 1.2 under the additional assumption 7 ⩽ | | + | | = | + | ⩽ − 4.\n## References (1)\n\n... Along these lines, we always have ⩾ −1 by the Cauchy-Davenport Theorem (Theorem 2.2). When = −1, Vosper's theorem [37,Theorem 8.1] [16] implies that Conjecture 1.2 holds without restriction. When = 0, Hamidoune and Rodseth [19] established Conjecture 1.2 under the additional assumption 7 ⩽ | | + | | = | + | ⩽ − 4. A more general result from [15] fully characterizes all and w